# 📖 LEARN BIBLE WITH ME
## Bible Learning Project in English

LEARN BIBLE WITH ME is a Bible education website that aims to help people learn the Holy Scriptures, understand Bible teachings, learn from people of faith, and apply Bible principles in everyday life.

This project was created using HTML5, CSS3 and Bootstrap 5.

## 👨💻 About the Author
- **Name:** HABIMANA PATRICK
- **University:** Bugema University
- **Study Program:** Software Engineering
- **Email:** habimanapatrick125@gmail.com
- **GitHub:** habimanapatrick125-eng

## 🎯 Project Goals
The goals of this project are:

- To help people learn the Bible in English.
- To explain important teachings of the Old Testament and the New Testament.
- To learn from examples of faith found in the Bible.
- To understand Bible warnings and teachings.
- To learn about the life and teachings of Jesus Christ.
- To help people apply Bible principles in everyday life.
- To provide a way to contact the project author.

## 📚 Website Pages
The project has the following pages:

| File | Description |
| --- | --- |
| `index.html` | Main page of the website |
| `old-testament.html` | Lessons about the Old Testament |
| `new-testament.html` | Lessons about the New Testament |
| `examples-of-faith.html` | Examples of faith from the Bible |
| `bible-warnings.html` | Warnings and teachings of the Bible |
| `life-of-jesus.html` | Life and teachings of Jesus Christ |
| `life-today.html` | Application of Bible teachings in life today |
| `contact-me.html` | Author contact |
| `Styles.css` | Design and styling of the website |

## 🛠️ Technologies Used
- **HTML5:** To create the structure of the website pages.
- **CSS3:** To style the website and arrange elements.
- **Bootstrap 5:** To create a layout that works on phones and computers.
- **Bootstrap Icons:** To add different icons.
- **Google Maps:** To show the general location of Goma.
- **Git and GitHub:** To save and manage the project code.
- **GitHub Pages:** To publish the website on the internet.

## 📂 Project Structure


## 🚀 How to Use the Project
1. Download or clone the project repository.
2. Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
3. Open the file `index.html` in a browser.
4. Use the website menu to visit different pages.
5. Make sure you have an internet connection to use Bootstrap CDN, the map and external images that need internet.

## 🌐 Publishing with GitHub Pages
To publish the website:

1. Upload all files to your GitHub repository.
2. Open that repository.
3. Go to Settings.
4. Select Pages.
5. Under Build and deployment, select Deploy from a branch.
6. Select the `main` branch and the `/ (root)` folder.
7. Click Save.
8. Wait for GitHub Pages to publish your website.
9. After publishing, you will be able to share your website link with other people.

